# The external toolchains this fork's boards download, from the mirrors at
# github.com/johnchia/firmware/releases/tag/toolchain-2026-08-28 (SigmaStar) and
# github.com/johnchia/firmware/releases/tag/toolchain-2026-09-25 (hisilicon).
#
# Buildroot has no hash for a custom external toolchain -- BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_URL
# is whatever the board says -- and prints "no hash file for ..." on every build
# instead. It does look here, though: pkg-generic's <pkg>_HASH_FILES searches
# $(BR2_GLOBAL_PATCH_DIR)/<pkg>/<pkg>.hash as well as the package's own
# directory, and BR2_GLOBAL_PATCH_DIR is general/package/all-patches. So the
# check can be supplied from this tree without patching Buildroot's.
#
# A line here turns a compiler that silently changed into a failed build. That
# is the whole point of the dated filenames: upstream publishes its toolchains
# on one tag and overwrites the assets in place, and a name that never changes
# cannot be hashed usefully.
#
# Locally computed, and identical to the bytes OpenIPC was serving on
# 2026-08-28 -- these are mirrored copies, not rebuilds.
sha256  44eacc941b9f319b3824164cfb90272ee939e6916dbe7b2ac7a167f1b83f8e6b  toolchain.sigmastar-infinity6e-20260828.tgz
sha256  61c4b9796decd55117e77e21c2a0473006d29003607b62ef4228babf861ec0bb  toolchain.sigmastar-infinity6c-20260828.tgz
sha256  59f1397302c1b6992481bcc4f45b2cbbdaf8590c1e3fab7b541e7e76469054db  toolchain.sigmastar-infinity6b0-20260828.tgz

# The hisilicon pair: hi3516ev200_raptor and hi3516ev300_raptor share the first,
# hi3516cv608_raptor and hi3516cv608_os04d10_raptorwifi the second (verified to
# carry arm-openipc-linux-musleabi gcc 13.3.0, the tuple and version the
# defconfig asks for).
#
# These two were pinned before they were mirrored, as upstream's undated assets
# on its moving `toolchain` tag, and that pin did its job: upstream rewrote
# both assets in place on 2026-09-14, and the next cold-cache build stopped
# with a hash mismatch instead of compiling the ports with a compiler nothing
# had been verified against. The mirror holds the bytes from before the
# rewrite -- the ev200 toolchain as fetched 2026-09-01, the cv6xx one as fetched
# 2026-09-07, both taken from the download caches of the trees that built the
# images on the boards -- so these lines are unchanged apart from the name.
sha256  75fa360224e3e0f7b1934d94e17dafa32c8d5a7745e8b6cf6e2e5ac1b9784641  toolchain.hisilicon-hi3516ev200-20260925.tgz
sha256  4bb9c409832f378e855af05a173f8b7b8957d39ffdb5b362cdbafb62b62e9e4a  toolchain.hisilicon-hi3516cv6xx-20260925.tgz
